---
description: Stable evidence, authority and safety invariants for the LP engine
alwaysApply: true
---

# Evidence & authority invariants

- ProductFacts / evidence are the only factual authority for copy.
- A seller claim is not an independently verified fact. DIRECT_SOURCE means "the source said it".
- Provenance (source URL, page category, unit, location) must survive every pipeline stage.
- No invented facts, no filler, no model world knowledge presented as product evidence.
- NOT_FOUND or closed evidence/topics cannot be resurrected downstream.
- Never weaken grounding, proposition binding, the closed-claim firewall, or health/policy rules.
- Operational facts (returns, shipping, format, fees) are restated, never strengthened into promises.
- No product-, slug-, or source-path-specific logic. Test generic rules with fictional products.
- Low evidence volume may legitimately produce a short LP. Maximize supported information, not word count.

# Process

- Deterministic generic defects: TRACE → CLASSIFY → FIX → TEST → REPLAY.
- New replay/evidence runs write to a new versioned directory; never overwrite earlier artifacts.
- Joint Genesis content and reference are frozen; its regression must pass after changes.

# Safety gates

- Public pages require publication approval; CONTENT_READY is not publication approval.
- No publish, deploy, live traffic, ads, or commit unless explicitly ordered.
- Paid model/API calls (Anthropic, OpenAI text/image, others) require explicit task authorization and a stated call budget.
